    "CHIR99021, a GSK3 inhibitor, may be relevant as a signaling-to-chromatin perturbation candidate because kinase inhibition can indirectly remodel histone modification patterns."
  ],
  "evidence_gap": "No direct measured histone-mark response values for EX527 in A375 are provided; donor selection is based on anchor-profile similarity, chromatin pharmacology, and the need to retrieve donor descriptions before any transfer. The PubChem description only confirms EX527 is a chlorinated tetrahydrocarbazole carboxamide and does not establish a histone-modifying mechanism."
